## Typography & Text Utilities

These classes control text alignment, size, color, transformation, spacing, and truncation.  
All typography utilities use the `ft-` prefix and are designed to maintain consistency across the application.

For global principles (BEM, `ft-` prefix, utility usage) review `css-styling.mdc`. This guide focuses on the typography utilities and how to apply them.

---

### Text Alignment

Use these classes to align text within an element.

| Class       | Description                 |
|--------------|-----------------------------|
| `ft-ta-s`    | Aligns text to the start (left in LTR languages). |
| `ft-ta-c`    | Centers the text.           |
| `ft-ta-e`    | Aligns text to the end (right in LTR languages). |

Example:
```html
<p class="ft-ta-c">Centered text</p>
```

### Font Size

Control text size with semantic utility classes.  
Font size values are defined in design tokens (`--ft-text-font-size-*`).

| Class          | Description                              |
|-----------------|------------------------------------------|
| `ft-fs-sm`      | Small text size.                         |
| `ft-fs-md`      | Default/medium text size.                |
| `ft-fs-lg`      | Large text size.                         |
| `ft-fs-lead`    | Emphasized leading text (headline-style).|
| `ft-fs-small`   | Small and bold text, useful for captions.|

Example:
```html
<p class="ft-fs-sm">Small text</p>
<p class="ft-fs-lg">Large text</p>
<p class="ft-fs-lead">Lead paragraph</p>
```

### Text Color

Use text color utilities to apply predefined theme colors.

| Class            | Description                        |
|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| `ft-tc-muted`     | Muted or secondary text color.     |
| `ft-tc-primary`   | Primary theme color.               |
| `ft-tc-info`      | Informational tone color.          |
| `ft-tc-success`   | Success/positive color.            |
| `ft-tc-danger`    | Error or alert color.              |
| `ft-tc-warning`   | Warning or attention color.        |

Example:

```html
<span class="ft-tc-success">Success message</span>
<span class="ft-tc-danger">Error message</span>
```

## Text Transformation

| Class           | Description             |
|-----------------|-------------------------|
| `ft-tt-lowercase` | Transforms text to lowercase. |
| `ft-tt-uppercase` | Transforms text to uppercase. |
| `ft-tt-capitalize` | Capitalizes the first letter of each word. |

### General Rules

- Use typography utilities instead of inline styles for consistency.
- Combine size, color, and alignment classes as needed.
- Prefer semantic combinations (e.g., ft-fs-lead ft-tc-primary) for emphasis.
- Avoid mixing multiple font-size classes on the same element.
